  "query_preview": "..\n(Monday through next Friday)\nIssued at 1238 PM CDT Sat Jul 25 2026\n\nUpper-level high pressure continues to dominate the area through the \nbeginning of next week. This will allow for continued triple-digit \nmaximum daily temperatures, mid- to high-70 degree low overnight \ntemperatures, and the continuation of heat products. However, toward \nthe end of next week, models begin to shift the upper-level high \npressure further west, placing the Panhandles in upper-level \nnorthwesterly flow. This pattern is typically favorable for active \nweather in the Panhandles, especially the northwest, as lee-side \nlow pressure systems and steering flow toward the Panhandles \ndevelop. There is still quite a bit of uncertainty in this scenario, \nand timing will become more clear as we get closer to the work week. \n\nFerguson",
